<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Helian Ding</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 432</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Helian Ding was the last emperor of Helian Xia, the brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/helian-chang">Helian Chang</a>, who rallied the remnants of the state after Chang's capture by Northern Wei in 428. In 431 he destroyed the Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> kingdom, but while crossing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a> he was captured by the Tuyuhun, who handed him to Northern Wei; he was executed in 432.</p></div>
